+**Relation pairs (per-target tracking):**
+
+Tracking modifiers accept relation pairs to track changes for a specific target:
+
+```typescript
+// Track additions/removals/data changes for a specific parent
+world.query(Added(ChildOf(parent)))
+world.query(Removed(ChildOf(parent)))
+world.query(Changed(ChildOf(parent)))
+```
+
+- The target `'*'` is a wildcard: `Added(ChildOf('*'))` fires for any target
+- Adding a second target and removing a non-last target are detected like first/last
+- Replacing the target of an exclusive relation emits both a removal and an addition
+- Destroying an entity fires pair-level removals for all active pairs
+- Opposite pair events on the same target within one observation window cancel each other
+- Pair modifiers combine with regular traits; all constraints are satisfied together
+- `entity.changed(Relation(target))` manually signals a pair-level change
+
 **Logical AND (default):**

 When multiple traits are passed to a tracking modifier, it uses logical AND. Only entities where **all** specified traits match the condition are returned:
